# scenarios/3b_stock_international.books: loaded by ledger_server into 3b_stock_international.db the first time it is picked,
# and again by Start over. Amounts are in cents.
title	3b. Stock, the international way: an asset until sold, then cost of sales
about	The international way (IFRS, the perpetual inventory): material bought for resale is not a cost when it is bought: it goes to Goods for resale, an asset. When it is sold, its cost moves from Goods for resale to Cost of sales, in the same period as the sale's revenue, so the profit on each sale shows: 5,000 less 3,000.
about	Here 5,000 of material is bought and 3,000 of it sold for 5,000; the 2,000 left simply stays in Goods for resale, and no count is needed to find the year's cost: Cost of sales is 3,000, so the profit is 2,000.
about	Scenario 3a has the same transactions done the Belgian way, through 604 Purchases and 609 Change in stock; the profit and the stock come out the same.
currency	USD
account	100000	equity	Share capital
account	550000	asset	Bank
account	440000	liability	Trade payables
account	340000	asset	Goods for resale
account	400000	asset	Trade receivables
account	700000	revenue	Sales
account	600000	expense	Cost of sales
